 up Mateo Mendia . Mendia’s clinical finish in the 63rd minute doubled the lead and seemingly put the result beyond doubt. The double-salvo forced the visitors into a flurry of substitutions, bringing on the likes of Jhojan Torres and Nahuel Lautaro Bustos in a desperate attempt to salvage a result. Late Drama and the Final Whistle As the clock wound down, the intensity rose once more. Santa Fe pushed forward with increased urgency, leading to a late yellow card for Daniel Torres and a frantic series of tactical changes from both dugouts. Just as the fourth official signaled for stoppage time, the visitors finally found a breakthrough. In the 94th minute, Emanuel Olivera turned provider for Franco Fagundez , who found the net to set up a nervous final few minutes for the home side. Despite the late pressure and the narrow margin, Platense held firm through seven minutes of added time. The referee’s final whistle confirmed a hard-fought victory for the hosts, rewarding their clinical edge in the second half and leaving Santa Fe to rue a period of defensive lapses that cost them dearly on the night. Key Match Events 13' : Yellow card – Victor Leandro Cuesta ( Santa Fe ) 57' : Goal – Tomas Nasif ( Platense ), Assist by Guido Mainero 63' : Goal – Mateo Mendia ( Platense ), Assist by Guido Mainero 90+4' : Goal – Franco Fagundez ( Santa Fe ), Assist by Emanuel Olivera",
